course: dictionary
lesson: 6026
title: One word, many meanings: meet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word meet has several meanings. You can find the right one by reading the words around it. «At his cousin's birthday they meet for real and nobody knows what to say.» Here meet means to come together in person and see each other for the first time.
explain: Look for clues. «The two roads meet at the bridge» means the roads join at one place. A meet can also be a sports event: a swim meet or a track meet. The clue is the word before it, not the word itself.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If «meet» means join, does the sentence still make sense? If you swap in «reach» for «meet the target» and the sentence still works, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Meet means to come together with someone in the same place.
fact: To meet someone can also mean to see them and get to know them for the first time, as in «nice to meet you».
fact: Lines, roads and rivers meet where they join.
fact: To meet a goal or a target means to reach it.
fact: A meet is a sports event, such as a swim meet or a track meet.
exercise: «At his cousin's birthday they meet for real and nobody knows what to say.» What does meet mean here? | To sing loudly together | *To come together in person | To break something by accident | To win a race
exercise: «The two roads meet at the bridge.» What does meet mean? | *Join at one place | Stop for a rest | Run away from each other | Go underground
exercise: Ella swam in the swim meet on Saturday. What is a swim meet? | A kind of swimming pool | A swimming lesson with a teacher | *A sports event | A type of fish
test: «Nice to meet you, Sam,» said Gran. What does meet mean here? | To hurry past someone | To lose someone in a crowd | To argue with someone | *To see someone for the first time and get to know them
test: The team worked hard and met their goal. What does met mean here? | Forgot | *Reached | Lost | Ran away from
exam: Which sentence uses meet to mean join? | Her hair is long and meets her shoulders | *Where the two rivers meet, the water is deep | We will meet at the station at noon | The swim meet starts at ten
